    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d565">

                <pb facs="0701" n="589" xml:id="pg589"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/574: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-27T17:00:00+08:00">May 27, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 27—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>220. Department’s 135, May 21, 5 p.m. Following telegram has been received from
                    the Consulate at Tsinanfu: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“May 27, 9 a.m. Resentment towards American silver program has appeared
                            here in mild form. Developments tending towards boycott American goods
                            have not yet appeared and will not likely appear unless sanctioned by
                            provincial authorities who in such matters would likely follow the
                            advice or lead of the Nanking authorities.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>To Nanking and Shanghai by mail.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
